// t_36492ad8 commit 1.  VISIBLE BINDING IDENTITY, NOT LOOKUP SUCCESS.
//
// The symbol table has no visibility cutoff for lookup: pass 1 puts every
// function in it, so a function declared AFTER a call is still "found".  The
// bookkeeping that records an unresolved callee has to ask whether a binding
// is VISIBLE AT THE CALL, not whether the name exists anywhere in the unit
// (review: codex, who found this on two different lookups in a row).
//
// ACCEPT: THE CONTROL THAT STOPS THE FIX FROM OVER-RECORDING.  The same body
// with f defined BEFORE it - f IS a visible binding at the call, the
// error-typed argument suppresses the call's diagnostics, and the later
// local is a legal shadow.  A fix that recorded every callee name
// regardless of visibility would refuse this (Fable).
float4 f(float4 t) { return t; }
float4 unused(float4 t) { f(missing); float f; return t; }
float4 main(float4 t : TEXCOORD0) : COLOR { return t; }
